# Recovered: the lifecycle batch log

Pulled off the production box on 2026-10-06, before pm2 rotated it away.

Why it is here. Deleting an account removes every trace of the person, which
is correct, but it meant the account total dropped with nothing to explain it.
These log lines were the only surviving record of what happened. From
2026-10-06 the deletionLog collection keeps a proper tally; everything before
that date exists only in this file.

What it says:

  - 128 daily batches, one per morning since launch.
  - 216 accounts purged in total. Every one of them an account that signed up,
    never verified, and passed the stale window.
  - One to three a day, every day. This was never a spike; it was a slow leak.
  - 26 of the lines carry a monthly send counter, which is the only
    dating available, since pm2 was not configured to timestamp. Those cover
    57 of the purges. The remaining 159 happened earlier and cannot
    be dated more precisely than "before September".

What changed because of it: the stale window went from 30 days to 45, and a
warning email now goes out a week before an account is removed. Until
2026-10-06 there was none.

Raw lines follow.

